# Code owners for Führerschein Hero.
#
# Later rules override earlier ones, so the catch-all comes first and the paths where a
# wrong change is actually dangerous come last. GitHub requests review from the owner of
# the most specific matching rule only.
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default owner for everything in the repository.
*                           @agusgonzaleznic

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Legal content. A wrong value here can cost someone the right to drive.
#
# rules.json holds every statutory period the deadline clock depends on, and the
# knowledge base is the sourced research the whole app rests on. Changes need a
# primary source and a re-read of the law, not just a passing review.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/src/data/                  @agusgonzaleznic
/docs/knowledge-base/       @agusgonzaleznic

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security posture. These two files ARE the app's defences.
#
# security.js holds sanitizeState() and safeUrl(), the import sanitiser and the URL
# scheme allowlist. index.html carries the Content-Security-Policy and the referrer
# policy. The CSP has no external origin in script-src or font-src because Leaflet
# and both fonts are vendored under src/assets/; re-adding a CDN would widen it
# again. A one-line edit to either file can silently remove a protection without
# failing anything visible.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/src/js/security.js         @agusgonzaleznic
/src/index.html             @agusgonzaleznic

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Licensing. The dual licence is what makes attribution enforceable, and the split
# between MIT code and CC BY 4.0 content is load-bearing. Never change without intent.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/LICENSE*                   @agusgonzaleznic

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supply chain. Workflows run with repository and Pages deployment access, so a
# change here can exfiltrate secrets or publish arbitrary content. Every action must
# stay pinned to a full commit SHA.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/         @agusgonzaleznic
